## 0. HEADLINE — main CSpace blocker FIXED & PROVEN; second blocker found

The task's PRIMARY diagnosed blocker — the fixed per-child-PD main CSpace
(CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2 = 8192 slots, single-page CNode backing) — was FIXED by a
multi-file vendored base-sel4 patch and PROVEN empirically within this
session (run1: seL4/core boots, falkon LAUNCHES from disk, lwIP DHCPs to
10.0.2.15). This disproves the prior "8192 main CSpace is the whole story"
model: with the main CSpace enlarged to 262144, falkon gets past every stage
that the 8192 config died at, and only falls at a NEW, previously-unseen
second blocker (§3).

  Acceptance (1) falkon_probe PASS: NOT MET — blocked by the SECOND
    blocker (vm_space PTE/pagemap selector pool, §3) AND, when vm_space
    enlargement was attempted, by a 16K-pool/device-memory interaction
    that also regressed the non-falkon scenarios (§4, §7).
  Acceptance (2) fixture GET: NOT MET — falkon dies before its HTTP GET.
  Acceptance (3) 5 regression scenarios: NOT MET — the shipped-attempt
    config HUNG sponge-boot (ahci started but part_block never detected
    the disk; §7), so the tree was REVERTED to pristine. The prior
    worker proved all 5 pass at the 16384 config.
  Acceptance (4) docs/11 ledger row #6: NOT added — reverted (no viable
    patch shipped this session).
  Acceptance (5) this evidence file: MET.

FINAL TREE STATE: PRISTINE (== HEAD bae5423d1b). All vendored changes were
reverted because the main-CSpace fix, while PROVEN to launch falkon+DHCP,
depends on a 16 KiB untyped-pool reservation whose carving breaks device
memory access on seL4 (regressing sponge-boot's ahci/disk path) — see §7.
The fix DESIGN (§1), the PROOF it launches falkon (run1 log, §1), the
SECOND-blocker diagnosis (§3), and the catalogue of failed vm_space
attempts (§4) are all preserved below so the next iteration does not
re-derive them. The path to a shippable fix is in §8.

