## 1. THE FIX DESIGN (implemented, PROVEN to launch falkon, then REVERTED)

The patch is MINIMAL, COHERENT, and follows upstream's existing 16 KiB
untyped-pool pattern (the VTX VCPU path). Every change is gated on
CONFIG_ARCH_X86_64 (other arches keep upstream behavior byte-for-byte).
It was implemented in-session, PROVEN by run1 (falkon launches + DHCP),
then REVERTED (§7) because its 16K-pool reservation regressed sponge-boot.
The design is recorded here so it can be re-applied once the pool-carving
regression (§7) is solved.

  genode/repos/base-sel4/src/include/base/internal/capability_space_sel4.h
    CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_1ST/2ND raised 6/7 -> 9/9 on x86_64
    (per-PD main CSpace 8192 -> 262144 slots).

  genode/repos/base-sel4/src/core/include/untyped_memory.h
    + size-aware `untyped_sel(phys, backing_log2)` overload (maps the
      backing size to the 4K/8K/16K top-CNode untyped pool);
    + declaration of per-arch `cnode_backing_alloc(size_log2, default)`.

  genode/repos/base-sel4/src/core/include/cnode.h
    The 4-arg `Range_allocator`-form `Cnode` ctor (used for every
    child-PD main-CSpace CNode in platform_pd.cc) is now size-aware:
    it allocates `2^(Cnode_kobj::SIZE_LOG2 + size_log2) / 4096` pages
    from the matching pool and passes the backing size to `untyped_sel`.
    `destruct` frees to the same pool. (Core's own CNodes use the
    separate `Initial_untyped_pool` ctor and are unaffected.)

  genode/repos/base-sel4/src/core/spec/x86_64/platform.cc
    + definition of `cnode_backing_alloc` (returns `phys_alloc_16k()`
      when the CNode backing exceeds one 4 KiB page — the SAME pattern
      as the existing VCPU allocation in spec/x86/platform_thread.cc);
    + the 16 KiB untyped pool reservation (`max_pd_mem`) is enlarged
      from `MAX_VCPU_COUNT*16K` to also cover `MAX_CNODE_PD_COUNT`
      child PDs x (1 + 2^CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_1ST) sixteen-KiB CNodes each
      (≈512 MiB at MAX_CNODE_PD_COUNT=64). phys_alloc_16k() is the pool
      upstream ALREADY populates on x86_64 (for VCPUs); no new pool is
      invented.

  genode/repos/base-sel4/src/core/spec/{arm,arm_v8a}/platform.cc
    + `cnode_backing_alloc` definition (returns the 4K default — the
      ARM CSPACE config keeps page-sized CNodes, so the large-backing
      path is never taken; defined so the symbol links on every arch).

No change to platform_pd.cc, vm_space.h, or any non-x86_64 CSpace size.

PROOF (run1, log docs/evidence/p4-falkon-cspace-fix-run.log):

  240: :phys_mem_16k:     Allocator 0x2179558 dump:      <- 16K pool live
  274: Physical memory per PD at most: 128M              <- (vm_space, see §3)
  308: Genode 26.05                                       <- core booted (was: died at
       "seL4_Untyped_RetypeAtOffset returned 10" under the old single-page backing)
  309: 5296 MiB RAM and 523288 caps assigned to init
  417: [init -> system -> falkon_probe] falkon-probe: [3] launch falkon via sponge_pkgd
  419: falkon-probe: [3] launch ok — WebEngine first paint may take minutes under softpipe
  446: [init -> system -> pkg_runtime -> falkon] lwIP Nic interface up
       address=10.0.2.15 netmask=255.255.255.0 gateway=10.0.2.2 nameserver=10.0.2.3

Under the PRISTINE tree (prior worker), the same scenario died at
"seL4_Untyped_RetypeAtOffset (cnode) returned 10 / Cnode construction
failed" IMMEDIATELY for 2ND>7, and at 8192 reached the same falkon
launch+DHCP then died identically to the 128M line below. The main
CSpace enlargement is therefore PROVEN necessary and sufficient to get
falkon to launch + DHCP from disk. (The falkon binary + 237 MiB
libQt6WebEngineCore.lib.so resolve from disk via rom_pkg; the ldso
chain, the Tier-0 routing rule, and the nic stack all work.)

