## 2. How the fix maps onto the prior diagnosis

Prior diagnosis (p4-cspace-falkon.log §3): "every child-PD CNode is
backed by exactly one 4 KiB untyped page; seL4 CTE = 32 B; one page
holds 128 = 2^7 CTEs; so 1ST/2ND are individually capped at 7; max
per-PD CSpace 2^14 = 16384; falkon needs strictly more."

The shipped fix addresses EXACTLY this:
  - 1ST/2ND -> 9/9 (each CNode now 2^(5+9) = 16 KiB, > one page);
  - the size-aware Cnode ctor backs each >4 KiB CNode from the 16 KiB
    untyped pool that upstream already populates on x86_64 (VTX), using
    the identical allocation+selector pattern the VCPU path proves
    (spec/x86/platform_thread.cc:39-52);
  - the 16 KiB pool reservation is grown to hold the CNode backings.

The prior diagnosis was CORRECT about the main CSpace. It did NOT,
however, surface the SECOND per-PD pool (vm_space) that also limits
falkon — see §3.

