## 3. THE SECOND BLOCKER — vm_space PTE/page-frame selector pool

PROVEN failure under the shipped main-CSpace fix (run1, lines 428-458):

  428: Warning: flush page table entries - mapping cache full - PD: init -> rom_pkg out of selector
  446: [falkon] lwIP Nic interface up address=10.0.2.15 ...
  455: Warning: flush page table entries - mapping cache full - PD: ... -> falkon out of selector
  458: [falkon] Error: stop because parent denied RM-session: ... cap_quota=2
  -> falkon_probe: FAIL (window never rendered); bounded timeout.

ROOT CAUSE (code path traced, not speculated):

  The "out of selector" + "mapping cache full" message is emitted by
  Core::Vm_space::_map_frame (vm_space.h:215-256), NOT by the main
  CSpace's Sel_alloc. Vm_space keeps a SEPARATE per-PD pool of
  PTE/page-frame selectors:

    vm_space.h enum { LEAF_CNODE_SIZE_LOG2=7, NUM_LEAF_CNODES_LOG2=5,
                      NUM_CNODE_3RD_LOG2=3 }
    => NUM_VM_SEL_LOG2 = 7+5+3 = 15  => 2^15 = 32768 selectors per PD.
    platform.cc:672 logs "Physical memory per PD at most: 128M"
      (= 32768 * 4096), confirming the pool size at runtime (run1:274).

  Each mapped 4 KiB page in a PD's address space consumes one selector
  from this pool (vm_space::_map_frame allocates a PTE selector, copies
  the page-frame cap into the leaf CNode). Falkon maps ~400 MiB of
  WebEngine+Qt6 libs eagerly (~100k frames) and rom_pkg caches the 509
  MiB payload as ROM dataspaces (~130k frames). BOTH exceed 32768
  independently. Vm_space's `_flush` eviction ("mapping cache full")
  cannot help because the working set is actively in use.

  This pool is INDEPENDENT of CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2 (the main CSpace). The
  shipped main-CSpace fix (262144 main slots) does not touch it. The
  prior diagnosis attributed "out of selector" to the main CSpace; the
  message prefix "flush page table entries - mapping cache full" shows
  it is actually vm_space's pool.

NUM_VM_SEL_LOG2 must rise so that max_page_frames()*4096 exceeds the
heaviest PD's mapping footprint (falkon ~100k frames; rom_pkg ~130k).
Target: NUM_VM_SEL_LOG2 = 18 (262144 selectors, 1 GiB max mappings/PD),
matching the enlarged main CSpace.

