## 6. REGRESSION status — NOT passing (the reason for the revert)

The shipped-attempt config REGRESSED sponge-boot (§7): with a 512 MiB
16K-pool reservation, init got only 180 MiB -> cached_fs_rom OOM; with a
proportional (total_ram/4 ≈ 247 MiB) reservation, init RAM was fine but
ahci started and part_block never detected the disk (vs the prior 16384
run which detected P1/P2/P3 and PASSed). The other four scenarios were
not re-run once sponge-boot failed. The prior worker's 16384 regression
logs (docs/evidence/p4-regress/) remain valid for THAT config; the
262144 config is the one that needs the §7 fix before it is regression-
clean.

