## 7. FINAL TREE STATE (hand-off) — PRISTINE / reverted

ALL vendored changes were REVERTED. The working tree matches HEAD
(bae5423d1b) exactly: `git status --short` is empty, `git diff` on
tracked files is empty. Nothing is committed (per instructions).

WHY REVERTED — the regression that sank the shipped attempt:

  The main-CSpace fix (§1) PROVENLY launches falkon + DHCP (run1). But it
  depends on a 16 KiB untyped-pool reservation (the size-aware Cnode ctor
  backs >4 KiB CNodes from phys_alloc_16k()). That reservation, when the
  tree was built and the regression set run, BROKE the non-falkon storage
  scenarios:

    sponge-boot (1G QEMU, docs/evidence/p4-regress-262144/sponge-boot.log):
      - With a FIXED 512 MiB reservation: init got only 180 MiB ->
        "cached_fs_rom: out of RAM during ELF loading" -> boot_probe FAIL.
      - With a PROPORTIONAL cap (reservation = total_ram/4 -> 247 MiB,
        verified by a temporary `cnode16k:` log line: "total_ram=991022K
        need=525568K reserved=253701632"; init then got 451 MiB): init RAM
        was fine, BUT ahci started ("--- Starting AHCI driver ---") and
        part_block NEVER detected the GPT partitions (vs the prior 16384
        run, docs/evidence/p4-regress/sponge-boot.log, where part_block
        reported P1/P2/P3 right after ahci and boot_probe PASSed). The
        boot hung at the acpi/ahci handshake for >15 min (bounded timeout).

  The ahci-no-disk failure is the SAME CLASS of issue as the §4 "device
  untyped" error: the 16 KiB pool carving interacts badly with seL4's
  physical-memory / device-memory management. Carving hundreds of MiB of
  16 KiB untypeds out of the initial untyped pool appears to either hand
  out bad (device) untypeds to the Cnode ctor or to starve/fragment the
  DMA-able memory the ahci driver needs. The pool population callback
  already skips device ranges, so the residual bug is subtle (likely a
  phys-address -> 16K-untyped-slot coherence issue or a DMA-pool
  interaction) and needs a seL4-cap-level trace to pin down.

  Because a patch that hangs sponge-boot is not shippable, the tree was
  reverted. The PROOF that the main CSpace fix launches falkon (run1 log)
  is preserved regardless of the revert.

Build: core is being rebuilt to pristine in the background (the build dir
       had the modified core; rebuild to match the reverted source).
       genode/build/x86_64/etc/build.conf left on KERNEL=sel4 BOARD=pc
       (git-ignored build dir; standard docs/11 §7.2 manual setting).

